<SleevePage sleeve="core" description="MSCI World, S&P 500 and STOXX Europe 600: daily candlestick charts, moving averages, RSI and MACD.">
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p class="lead">
      Three broad equity indices that, between them, cover most of the world's listed companies by value. They are the
      kind of funds a long-term investor holds for decades.
    </p>
    <div class="note">
      <strong>Watch the overlap.</strong> The United States weighs about two-thirds of the MSCI World (68% at the end of September 2026, source: MSCI), so holding both the
      MSCI World and the S&amp;P 500 doubles down on American large caps. The STOXX Europe 600 rebalances towards
      Europe. Knowing what overlaps is the first step in understanding real diversification.
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</SleevePage>

